sequence Night Signal Chain

tag Owner as o
  Crown red
  Guild blue

[Flagship] o: Crown
  Lookout
  [Gun Deck] o: Guild
    PowderRoom
    RangeMaster
  Helm
  QuarterMaster

[Harbour Watch] o: Crown
  [Watchtower] o: Guild
    BeaconKeeper
    TideGauge

[Signal Chain]
  Runner o: Crown
  [Cipher Room] collapsed
    CipherClerk
    CodeBook

== Sighting ==
Lookout -sail on the horizon-> Helm
Helm -range the target-> RangeMaster

note right of RangeMaster
  Bearing and elevation are
  read off the same glass, so
  one clerk owns both numbers

RangeMaster -draw two charges-> PowderRoom
PowderRoom -charges ready-> RangeMaster
RangeMaster -laid and ready-> QuarterMaster

== Raising the Alarm ==
QuarterMaster -light the beacon-> BeaconKeeper
BeaconKeeper -read the tide-> TideGauge
TideGauge -water is making-> BeaconKeeper
BeaconKeeper -beacon lit-> Runner

== Passing the Word ==
Runner -carry the dispatch-> CipherClerk
CipherClerk -look up the night code-> CodeBook
CodeBook -tonight's cipher-> CipherClerk
CipherClerk -sealed dispatch-> Runner
Runner -word is away-> QuarterMaster
